    "**Why chunks?** Sampling memory grows with frames x pixels. The clip is cut into pieces of **Frames per chunk** (21), each is restored on its own, and neighbours share 2 latent frames (8 frames) that are crossfaded. On the test clip the motion of the result follows the source frame by frame, with no jump at the joins. The template leaves the split off; it is always on here, in `manual` mode (`auto` sizes chunks from free VRAM and was not run)."
   ]
  },
