    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "title": "How to use · v1.0.0",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## How to use · SeedVR2 Upscaler (video) v1.0.0\n\n**What it does:** makes a video bigger and restores detail with SeedVR2 3B (int8), one step per chunk of frames. Sound and frame rate of the clip are kept. No prompt. Core ComfyUI nodes only.\n\n1. **Your inputs**: pick your clip in **Video to upscale** (it opens with the name of the test clip, which a fresh ComfyUI does not have). **Upscale factor** 2 doubles width and height; 1 restores without enlarging. **Start at second** and **Seconds to upscale** cut a part out (0 and 0 = the whole clip).\n2. **Models**: download the two files from the note below. Nothing to change here.\n3. **Cut, enlarge + encode**: the frames are enlarged with lanczos first; SeedVR2 then works at the final size.\n4. **Restore in chunks**: 1 step, CFG 1, euler / simple per chunk, from the template. **Frames per chunk** (21, must be 4n+1) and the **Seed** sit here: leave both.\n5. **Decode + colour match**: `lab` pulls the colours back to the original. The template uses `none`; `none` was not run here.\n6. **Save**: MP4 in `ComfyUI/output/video/`.\n\n**What to expect** (RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell SFF Edition 24 GB, ComfyUI 0.45.3)\n- 480x864 clip, 124 frames (5.2 s), factor 2 = 960x1728: 4 min 25 s with no limit (VRAM 11.8 GiB), 4 min 30 s in a 12 GiB budget (10.5 GiB), 4 min 33 s in a 10 GiB budget (9.3 GiB). All three look the same (45 to 47 dB PSNR against each other).\n- System RAM: the ComfyUI process peaked at 19.0 to 20.3 GiB for this clip. 32 GB of system RAM is the safe size; less was not tried.\n- VRAM = peak of the ComfyUI process in nvidia-smi, in GiB (MiB / 1024; a 12 GB card has 12.0). Budget runs: a second ComfyUI started with `--reserve-vram` so that it may use only 12 or 10 GiB. Not verified on a real 12 GB card.\n\n**Good to know**\n- Try 2 seconds first (**Seconds to upscale** = 2). Time grows with result size and clip length.\n- SeedVR2 redraws fine texture; small faces and text can change. Compare before you keep it.\n"
   ]
  },
